// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    The Pratfall
// @category Slapstick / Comedy
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/The_Pratfall
// @version  1.3
// @domain    Narrative
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): a comic physical fall — named for an archaic word for the buttocks — and
// one of the most fundamental forms of Schadenfreude; a stock gag of the circus clown, Older Than
// Radio, perfected on the vaudeville stage and in silent film. Rides the rhetoric module's
// Appraise_Comic: a hurt body FRAMED comic lands as funny — the pain is not the point. The Pratfall
// is the specifically PHYSICAL, DIGNITY-DEFLATING case of that framing — the pompous brought low by
// gravity, the exaggerated tumble. It is the same mishap as a Tear Jerker's stumble; only the
// author's framing differs (comic vs. earnest), which is exactly the axis rhetoric.trl turns on:
// frame the identical fall earnest and it stings (Appraise_Earnest -> audience [#Moved]) instead.


// === IMPORTS & ASSOCIATIONS ===
import "trl/modules/rhetoric.trl"          // Appraise_Comic -> audience [#Amused]

assoc pratfall -> [
  rhetoric       : "the physical comic-framing case of",
  audience       : "buys Schadenfreude laughter from the",
  rule_of_funny  : "is the bodily-fall sibling of"
]


// === ONTOLOGY ===
// The dignity-deflation: a dignified body undone by gravity, the harm framed harmless.
imply Pratfall -> [Slapstick, Comedy, Schadenfreude, Narrative]


// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// Naming rule: a fallen, dignified body whose fall the author frames comic IS the Pratfall — the
// pompous brought low for a laugh, the pain conspicuously not the point.
rule Pratfall {
  when:
    char $c [+Hurt] [+Dignified]
    evt  $f [&Frames(agent=author, target=$c, as=comic)]
  then:
    $f [+Pratfall]
}


// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: Buster Keaton — the great stone face takes a tumble (silent film, 1920s) ===
// Keaton, the source's named master of the form, plays the stoic gentleman in coat and porkpie hat —
// the picture of unshakable dignity. He hits a patch and goes down hard, deadpan to the last; the
// exaggerated tumble (his backward-roll specialty) is rehearsed to the inch precisely so it reads as
// funny and not as injury. The dignity is the setup; gravity is the punchline; the house roars.

// BUSTER (the great stone face) — dignified gentleman, porkpie hat
char buster [+Hurt] [+Dignified]

scene the_tumble {
  beat 1 {
    evt the_spill [&Frames(agent=author, target=buster, as=comic)]
    // Appraise_Comic (rhetoric) -> audience [#Amused];  Pratfall tags the framed fall
    // (frame the identical spill as=earnest and Appraise_Earnest -> audience [#Moved] instead)
  }
}
